{"title":"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The lengths in inches of the three sides of each of four triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e8e8646c9d6b54459ef7914ce0191d8a9e8aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I, II, III$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> are as follows: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83606504493d9199f439a86f14de03005c6cf97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{rlrl} \\hbox{I}&amp; 3,\\ 4,\\ \\hbox{and}\\ 5\\qquad &amp; \\hbox{III}&amp; 7,\\ 24,\\ \\hbox{and}\\ 25\\\\  \\hbox{II}&amp; 4,\\ 7\\frac{1}{2},\\ \\hbox{and}\\ 8\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad &amp; \\hbox{IV}&amp; 3\\frac{1}{2},\\ 4\\frac{1}{2},\\ \\hbox{and}\\ 5\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"353\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Of these four given triangles, the only right triangles are \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5c962a2bb0dd9a52da98ec4efdb5733eaf2568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)  I and II}\\qquad  \\text{(B)  I and III}\\qquad \\text{(C)  I and IV} \\quad \\\\ \\text{(D)  I, II, and III} \\qquad \\text{(E)  I, II, and IV }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's test out the four triangles:\n</p><p>I: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2eb725cd78ee115163f9339dc4df00bc7bd4304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 + 4^2 = 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> (true)\n</p><p>II: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582a12ada98f82517d75191a10e06db2734cd4f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 + 7.5^2 = 8.5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> (true)\n</p><p>III: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5e002e6798c26c5708d7991054f19343a820f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2 + 24^2 = 25^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The only answer choice with I, II, and III in the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec5fac156ee8301b7c112d9b6891f4701291f32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{D} \\rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"23\" /> I, II, and III.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170819\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.007 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1858/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15541:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170819 and revision id 222799. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}